---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const updated = "September 18, 2026";

const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/privacy#webpage",
    url: "https://thisishowwesee.com/privacy",
    name: "Privacy Policy — How We See LLC",
    dateModified: "2026-09-18",
    publisher: { "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/#business" },
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — How We See LLC"
  description="How We See LLC's privacy policy: what this website collects, what the software built here does with Google account data, and how to get in touch."
  schema={schema}
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy <span class="accent">Policy</span></h1>
      <p>
        How We See LLC is a one-person product development consultancy run by Howie Seay.
        This page covers two separate things: what this website does with your information,
        and what the software built under this name does with Google account data.
        Last updated {updated}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / This website</p>
      <h2>The site collects nothing</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">
        thisishowwesee.com is a set of static pages. There is no analytics script, no tracking
        pixel, no advertising network and no cookie set by this site. Nobody is building a profile
        of your visit, because there is nothing here that could.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        The site is hosted on Vercel, and like every web host, Vercel records standard server logs
        containing IP addresses, timestamps and requested URLs. Those logs exist to keep the
        service running and to stop abuse.
        <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Vercel's privacy policy</a>
        governs them. Fonts load from Google Fonts, which means Google sees the request for the
        font file.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        If you email me, I keep the email. I do not add correspondents to a mailing list, and I do
        not sell, rent or share contact details with anyone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Software and Google account data</p>
      <h2>Private tools, one user</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">
        Some software built under the How We See name signs in with Google and reads Google
        account data. Seay Mail MCP is one such application. These are private tools that Howie
        Seay runs on his own computer, against his own Google accounts. They are not products,
        they are not offered to the public, and they have no other users.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        These applications may request access to Gmail, Google Drive, Google Calendar, Google
        Docs, Google Sheets, Google Tasks, Google Contacts, Google Chat and Google Apps Script.
        Access tokens and any retrieved content stay on the local machine. Nothing is copied to a
        server operated by How We See LLC, because there is no such server. Nothing is transmitted
        to a third party, used for advertising, sold, or used to train a machine learning model.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        Access can be withdrawn at any time from the
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google account
        permissions page</a>, which revokes the tokens immediately.
      </p>

      <div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <p class="feature-kicker">Limited Use</p>
          <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">
            How We See LLC's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
            <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google
            API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <p class="feature-kicker">Retention</p>
          <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">
            Tokens live in a credentials file on one laptop and are deleted when the tool is
            removed or access is revoked. No copy exists anywhere else.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Consulting work</p>
      <h2>Client material</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">
        Consulting engagements often involve confidential technical and commercial information.
        That material is handled under whatever agreement governs the engagement, and the terms of
        that agreement take priority over this page. Client information is never used to train a
        machine learning model and is never shared with another client.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Contact</p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">
        Write to <a href="mailto:howie@thisishowwesee.com">howie@thisishowwesee.com</a> with any
        question about this policy, or to ask what information is held about you. If this policy
        changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
